color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  1 big thing: Anthropic IPO spikes, then settles </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td> <img src=\"https://images.axios.com/ahMDnEKYx2HybzsD1ufkgF61QNU=/0x0:1280x720/2026/10/22/1792698853047.gif\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" id=\"item02\" alt=\"Animated photo illustration of a closeup of Dario Amodei's face. In the lenses of his glasses, a stock chart can be seen, with a trend line moving up and down from left to right.\"> </td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.3\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#848484\"> <p>Photo illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios. Photo: Samyukta Lakshmi/Bloomberg via Getty Images</p> </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><p><strong>AI giant Anthropic opened for trading today</strong> in the biggest public stock offering ever, despite investor fears of a possible AI bubble and anxiety that the technology threatens lives and livelihoods.</p><ul><li><strong>Anthropic shares </strong>began trading at $111.50, spiking more than 30% above the initial public offering price.</li><li><strong>They fell to</strong> around $98 as of midafternoon.</li></ul><p><strong>💰 A day earlier,</strong> the company priced its IPO at $83 per share. </p><ul><li><strong>That was enough to value</strong> the entire business at $1.5 trillion, surpassing SpaceX as the largest IPO on record. </li><li><strong>At the start of trading, </strong>Anthropic's valuation leaped to $2.01 trillion.</li></ul><p><strong>Between the lines: </strong>The initial price was surprisingly high given investor worries since the stunning ouster of AI's chief promoter, Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang, amid a possible Chinese spying scandal.</p><p><strong>📈 What we're watching: </strong>What happens to the share price before today's 4 p.m. ET close.</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.403596/aHR0cHM6Ly9hcG5ld3MuY29tL2FydGljbGUvYW50aHJvcGljLWlwby1uYXNkYXEtYWktYjZhNzRiODk0OTAyMTIwN2RjMTYyZmNjODc2YzQ2NDk_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NwbSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB86793577\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Go deeper</em></a><em> ... </em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.403596/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tLzIwMjYvMTEvMTkvYW50aHJvcGljLWlwby1jbGF1ZGUtY3J1c2g_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NwbSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBe59e111b\" target=\"_blank\"><em>More from Dan Primack</em></a><em>.</em></li></ul></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.403596/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtcG0tZGEwYWE4ZjEtYjI0My00NjRkLTkxMGEtNTJlZmM4M2I4ZTg3Lmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0QxJTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3RvcnkxJnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zcG0mc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBbaff9f75\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.403596/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9pbnRlbnQvdHdlZXQ_\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-x-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Tweet this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-linkedin-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Post to LinkedIn\"></a>  <a href=\"mailto:?subject=From Axios: 1 big thing: Anthropic IPO spikes, then settles&body=teruyuki%40hh.iij4u.or.jp%20has%20shared%20an%20Axios%20story%20with%20you%3A%0A%0A1 big thing: Anthropic IPO spikes, then settles%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2Fnewsletters%2Faxios-pm-da0aa8f1-b243-464d-910a-52efc83b8e87.html%3Fchunk%3D1%26utm_term%3Demshare%23story1\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-email-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Email this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-sms-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Text this Story\"></a></td></tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  2. 🤖 Bots fueled outage conspiracies </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><div align=\"center\"><!--[if mso]><img alt='' src='https://images.axios.com/tzUYP9wvaraegwF6L5tbDSzVYq0=/fit-in/1116x1300/2021/01/11/220014-1610402414642.png' style='display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;' width='558' /><![endif]--><!--[if !mso]><!--><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://images.axios.com/tzUYP9wvaraegwF6L5tbDSzVYq0=/fit-in/1116x1300/2021/01/11/220014-1610402414642.png\" style=\"display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;\" width=\"100%\"/><!--<![endif]--></div> <div class=\"bodytext\" style=\"font-size:13px; font-family:'Gordita',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; color:#848484; margin-bottom:20px;\">Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios</div><p><strong>Bot accounts helped spread </strong>conspiracy theories about the recent major tech outages, <em>Axios' Sam Sabin reports from exclusive new research.</em></p><p><strong>🖼️ The big picture: </strong>Purveyors of disinformation appear to be exploiting public anxiety over the outages and fragile infrastructure, amplifying suspicions of coordinated cyberattacks and government cover-ups.</p><ul><li><strong>It's unclear </strong>who's behind these accounts. But the pattern shows that when technology failures lack substantive explanations, bot networks will fill the void to manufacture panic.</li></ul><p><strong>By the numbers: </strong>Suspected bots accounted for roughly 30% of posts promoting conspiracy theories about several recent tech outages, according to data from social media monitoring firm PeakMetrics.</p><ul><li><strong>During Microsoft's outage,</strong> bots accounted for 26% of conspiratorial posts.</li></ul><p><strong>🤳  Bots accounted for 34%</strong> of conspiracy-related posts during Friday's Workday outage, compared with 27% of other posts.</p><ul><li><strong>Likely bot accounts</strong> also made up 31% of conspiracy-related posts about Bank of America's outage, and 28% of posts linking Chase's outage to other disruptions.</li></ul><p><strong><em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.403596/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tLzIwMjYvMTEvMTkvdGVjaC1vdXRhZ2VzLWJvdHMtY29uc3BpcmFjaWVzP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zcG0mc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB6e5d3d1f\" target=\"_blank\">Go deeper</a>.</em></strong></p></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.403596/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtcG0tZGEwYWE4ZjEtYjI0My00NjRkLTkxMGEtNTJlZmM4M2I4ZTg3Lmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0QyJTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3RvcnkyJnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zcG0mc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aCdd08868e\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.403596/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9pbnRlbnQvdHdlZXQ_\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-x-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Tweet this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-linkedin-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Post to LinkedIn\"></a>  <a href=\"mailto:?subject=From Axios: 🤖 Bots fueled outage conspiracies&body=teruyuki%40hh.iij4u.or.jp%20has%20shared%20an%20Axios%20story%20with%20you%3A%0A%0A🤖 Bots fueled outage conspiracies%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2Fnewsletters%2Faxios-pm-da0aa8f1-b243-464d-910a-52efc83b8e87.html%3Fchunk%3D2%26utm_term%3Demshare%23story2\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-em