idth=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.403596/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9pbnRlbnQvdHdlZXQ_\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-x-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Tweet this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-linkedin-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Post to LinkedIn\"></a>  <a href=\"mailto:?subject=From Axios: ⚡️ Catch me up&body=teruyuki%40hh.iij4u.or.jp%20has%20shared%20an%20Axios%20story%20with%20you%3A%0A%0A⚡️ Catch me up%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2Fnewsletters%2Faxios-pm-da0aa8f1-b243-464d-910a-52efc83b8e87.html%3Fchunk%3D3%26utm_term%3Demshare%23story3\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-email-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Email this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-sms-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Text this Story\"></a></td></tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  4. 👨‍🏫 1 for the road: The GTA professor </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><div align=\"center\"><!--[if mso]><img alt='' src='https://images.axios.com/zFZBmPJy4br7gRUNy-MF6dBo6bg=/fit-in/1116x1300/2025/09/19/1758305646309.jpeg' style='display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;' width='558' /><![endif]--><!--[if !mso]><!--><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://images.axios.com/zFZBmPJy4br7gRUNy-MF6dBo6bg=/fit-in/1116x1300/2025/09/19/1758305646309.jpeg\" style=\"display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;\" width=\"100%\"/><!--<![endif]--></div> <div class=\"bodytext\" style=\"font-size:13px; font-family:'Gordita',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; color:#848484; margin-bottom:20px;\">Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios</div><p><strong>University of Tennessee history professor</strong> Tore Olsson is using the hit gaming franchise Grand Theft Auto to dive into bigger questions about modern America, <em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.403596/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL2xvY2FsL25hc2h2aWxsZT91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc3BtJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB04a99749\" target=\"_blank\">Axios Nashville's</a> Adam Tamburin reports.</em></p><p><strong>🎮 Olsson's \"Grand Theft America\" course</strong> isn't the gamer gab session some students might expect.</p><ul><li><strong>He estimates</strong> that no more than 10% of class time is devoted to discussing fictional events from the games.</li><li><strong>The rest delves</strong> into globalization, mass incarceration, the war on drugs and other forces that have shaped America since 1980.</li></ul><p><strong>🤯 Olsson tells Axios: </strong>\"I'm getting them in the door with pop culture ... and then convincing them to care, and then trying to blow their minds with content and approaches and perspectives that they've never considered previously.\"</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.403596/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL2xvY2FsL25hc2h2aWxsZS8yMDI2LzExLzE5L2dyYW5kLXRoZWZ0LWF1dG8tZ3RhLWhpc3RvcnktY2xhc3MtdXQtcHJvZmVzc29yP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zcG0mc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB5f869bc2\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Go deeper</em></a><em> ... </em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.403596/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL25ld3NsZXR0ZXJzL2xvY2FsP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zcG0mc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB7fdcd6d6\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Get Axios Local</em></a><em>.</em></li></ul></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.403596/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtcG0tZGEwYWE4ZjEtYjI0My00NjRkLTkxMGEtNTJlZmM4M2I4ZTg3Lmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0Q0JTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3Rvcnk0JnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zcG0mc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aE775d46ce\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.403596/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9pbnRlbnQvdHdlZXQ_\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-x-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Tweet this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48526790.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><im